# shell: desktop
# board: net
# The board's window over an address, not a cable.  The board dials this
# desktop, which is listening rather than scanning ports, and its window
# comes up on the desk; its shell comes over the same connection, so the
# board is mounted under /devices as a board on a cable would be, its
# manifest read a page at a time.  This needs the board on the cable
# flashed with
# TIKU_KIT_NET_ENABLE=1 TIKU_KITS_NET_LINK_IP_ENABLE=1 TIKU_APPL_GUI=1
# TIKU_APPL_GUI_IP=1 TIKU_APPL_DRAW_DEMO=1, and the harness carries its
# connection here (see run.sh's net lane).
wait 400
note the board's window is on the desktop, beside the fixture's folder
expect-windows 2
expect-title Board window
note the board's shell came over the connection: it is mounted by name
expect-read /devices tiku
expect-read /devices/tiku/sys/device/name tiku
note the button counts: a press crosses the connection and its redraw
note comes back the same way
click 421 390
wait 45
expect-narrate Pressed 1 time
shot /tmp/trk_boardnet.png
quit
